This is true that there is no reason for DCE to run on the DNS machine. My point
was, if you want to use the smit tool that IBM gives you to do the intercell
setup, you have to install DCE software on that machine, otherwise you won't
see DCE menus from smit.

Of course, as someone pointed out, you can always ftp that particular script from
another machine and just run the script. You can also ftp the named database file
to a machine which runs DCE and use smit to run the intercell script there, then
ftp the database file back.

And you can always manually edit the named database file. Many people did it (I 
am one of them).

