In order to get a disklabel on a "foreign" disk, use the
following command:

	% disklabel -r -w /dev/rrz.. foobar

The disklabel *requires* a disktype, but if the disktype is not
known, the disklabel program will read all parameters from the
disk itself. So, supposing You have no disktab entry named "foobar",
the above command does create the "right" disklabel!

Lukas

P.S. It would be nice, if this would be stated in the documentation...


