pthread_getexpiration_np in order to figure out the end time, and I hate
using _np routines.  Another part of the problem with this approach is
that the timing is less reliable.  I have to determine the time for the next
read before commencing the read, so that my interval isn't (time for read to
complete) + interval instead of just the given interval.  Also, if a network
event causes a read to take longer than the interval, I will get two reads,
one immediately after the other, with the next read thereafter commencing
at a new offset (e.g. I might get reads starting at 10 sec, 20 sec, 30 sec,
42 sec, 52 sec, etc.)  For my current purposes, this shouldn't be a problem,
but I'd like to code something more reliable if possible.

- Brad
