|> Any decent program should accept these characters like any other. There 
|> is one strange thing with this key on at least some DEC machines. It only 
|> works if pressed in conjunction with the space key (what a queer idea!), 

This bit of 'oddity' is due to the lack of an 'Alt' or 'Meta' key on the 
earlier dec keyboards. As the 'Compose' key is unused in many locales,
the 'Compose' key is mapped instead as an 'Alt' key. Xlib was modified to
accept Alt-space as a compose sequence introducer in order to maintain
the compose functionality. This way, you can have both with the older keyboards,
an Alt key and a Compose key. 

On the newer style keyboards there is both an Alt and a Compose key and
so the workaround is less important.

The next generation of machines will be using PC style keyboards. These
keyboards don't have a labeled compose key. You can use Xmodmap to bind
one of the two Alt or one of the two Ctrl key to be Compose if you wish,
otherwise..... Alt -space will still be there.

/Dave


