>call/response message pair for the RPC to the RPCD, transport connect
>to the server, call/response message pair for the RPC to the server.

(Hesitant to correct Nat...) for RPC over datagram protocols this isn't
true.  The client connects to the rpcd, the rpcd forwards the packet to
the correct server, and the first reply back from the server (an ack, nak,
send more data, etc) contains the fully-bound endpoint of the server
which is used by the client for future communications over that handle.
