No! The letter "�" is a LETTER, not a ligature. It is a single letter
that visually resembles the letters "a" and "e" melted together, but
is is a letter in its own right, NOT a ligature.

This is not particularly relevant to this group, or to this
discussion, and I apologize. But this misunderstanding keeps on giving
us trouble. First the "�" was dropped from the Courier PostScript fonts,
since they don't contain ligatures, and then it was omitted from the
drafts of ISO 10646 (but luckily made it into the final version).

And yes, "�" is used in Norwegian as well. And Norwegian is a language
in its own right, not a dialect of Danish. It just seems that way.


