In article <2qtlad$ko9@falcon.ccs.uwo.ca>, jwkhong@csd.uwo.ca (James W. Hong) writes:
|> We are trying to add inter-cell communication capability to our AIX DCE
|> platform.  According to AIX DCE administration guide, we need to add an entry
|> in DNS (Domain Name Service).  Unfortunately, the IBM documentation is not good
|> enough to help and it appears to insist on (or expect to) use IBM-specific mods
|> to the DNS record structure.
